  "claims": [
    "The original mixed Circuit syntax has an explicit single-state evaluator. Tensor executes left and then right with the same evolving state; wires copy/discard port values only.",
    "The old state-independent models and checked roots lift with unchanged port laws.",
    "A root equality universal in state and input lifts through all existing seq/tensor Step placements, preserving arbitrary correlated past and original state/input; condition repair uses the updated checked model.",
    "A shared-bit/log example distinguishes continuous execution from restarting both children, rejects unrestricted exchange, distinguishes copying a produced value from executing the effect twice, and retains state/log effects when discarding output.",
    "For one common stochastic transition function, every mixed schedule is exactly the corresponding uninterrupted execution, paired with deterministic port output.",
    "A single schematic adjacent-chunk fusion rule has a concrete checked model and preserves full state in every mixed placement.",
    "Specialization to actual native caller frames retains oracle state, all machine tapes/control and complete bit request/response transcript across chunk boundaries.",
    "Any optimized native mixed schedule of total horizon 286 inherits stopping and four additional oracle calls for arbitrary typed oracle state and prior trace.",
    "Any old schedule of horizon 343 and optimized schedule of horizon 286 satisfy the existing complete-frame PC relocation correspondence.",
    "A concrete tensor/copy/discard schedule splits 286 into 100 and 186 transitions and has the exact complete native-frame law of the uninterrupted caller.",
    "Sampling the original key distribution connects any such schedule to every preparation-order full MAC law and the inherited fixed-attack forgery upper bound 1/256."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "The stateful tensor is explicitly left-first; arbitrary effectful interchange is not an axiom.",
    "The same transition function/program/oracle runs through every clocked box. This is not arbitrary program switching or a general native compiler.",
    "Clocked-box ports contain empty values. General typed port values belong to the separate generic Stateful.Model.",
    "Clocked boxes are execution durations, not the crypto proof-transformation boxes of the existing MACNormalization signature.",
    "This implements scheduling semantics and one local fusion schema, not a complete finite higher critical basis for the full mixed crypto/fusion/wiring presentation.",
    "Local stateful root validity is an explicit proof obligation. Updating a model/its kernels or native contract is not discharged by dependency-set repair alone.",
    "Old-to-new code refinement is a separate final-frame correspondence, not equality of their clock processes or an already integrated stateful rewriting root.",
    "The 286 quantity is a transition horizon/bound; absorbing halted-state steps and proof traversal are not new actual useful-work costs.",
    "Native oracle internals and initial key sampling are external. The compact native oracle backend remains to be connected.",
    "The cryptographic upper bound is inherited for the existing fixed attack with 8 messages and 256 tags. No asymptotic or arbitrary-adversary result.",
    "No proof-size, total checking-time, or higher-dimensional necessity advantage over ordinary shared proof has been demonstrated; these proofs use ordinary structural induction and local composition."
  ],
  "concrete_contract": {
    "same_program_all_chunks": true,
    "tensor_order": "left then right on returned shared state",
    "example_chunks": [
      100,
      186
    ],
    "optimized_total_horizon": 286,
    "old_total_horizon": 343,
    "extra_oracle_calls": 4,
    "native_frame_components_retained": [
      "opaque oracle state",
      "control and all tapes",
      "full reverse bit transcript"
    ],
    "key_domain_messages": 8,
    "tag_cardinality": 256,
    "finite_success_upper_bound": "1/256"
  },
  "novelty": {
    "status": "unconfirmed",
    "interpretation": "Necessary concrete shared-state/native foundation, not claimed as new state semantics, higher coherence, security bound or proof compression. Full mixed finite local basis, code-changing reduction interpretation, observational contracts, complete runtime, fair total costs and primary-theorem priority remain open."
  },
